---
/**
 * Discovery Section - Phase 4.2
 *
 * EDA visualizations with scroll-reveal animations.
 * Presents key insights from exploratory data analysis.
 */
import Section from '../ui/Section.astro';
import Container from '../ui/Container.astro';
import ImageReveal from '../ui/ImageReveal.astro';
import {edaImages} from '../../lib/images';
---

<Section id="discovery" background="gradient" align="start">
  <Container size="wide" className="py-8">
    {/* Section header */}
    <div class="text-center mb-16 animate-fade-up">
      <h2 class="headline-section text-white mb-4">Discovery</h2>
      <p class="body-large text-slate-300 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        Exploring patterns in 31 million flights to uncover what drives delays.
      </p>
    </div>

    {/* Discovery sub-sections */}
    <div class="discovery-grid">
      {/* Sub-section 1: Airline delays */}
      <div class="discovery-item animate-fade-up">
        <div class="discovery-content">
          <h3 class="headline-subsection text-white mb-3">
            Which Airlines Delay Most?
          </h3>
          <p class="body-default text-slate-300 mb-4">
            Delay rates vary significantly across carriers. Frontier and JetBlue show
            the highest delay percentages, while Hawaiian Airlines performs best. This
            suggests operational factors beyond weather play a significant role.
          </p>
          <div class="insight-callout">
            <span class="insight-icon">💡</span>
            <span class="insight-text">
              Low-cost carriers tend to have tighter turnaround times, correlating with
              higher delay rates.
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="discovery-visual">
          <ImageReveal
            src={edaImages.delaysByAirline}
            alt="Flight delays by airline showing percentage of delayed flights for each carrier"
            caption="Percentage of flights delayed by carrier (2015-2019)"
          />
        </div>
      </div>

      {/* Sub-section 2: Geographic patterns */}
      <div class="discovery-item reverse animate-fade-up">
        <div class="discovery-content">
          <h3 class="headline-subsection text-white mb-3">
            Geographic Patterns
          </h3>
          <p class="body-default text-slate-300 mb-4">
            Flight volume concentrates around major hubs: Atlanta, Chicago O'Hare,
            Dallas-Fort Worth, Denver, and Los Angeles. These hub airports see the
            most flights but also experience cascading delay effects.
          </p>
          <div class="insight-callout">
            <span class="insight-icon">📍</span>
            <span class="insight-text">
              Hub airports create network effects where a single delay can propagate
              across the system.
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="discovery-visual">
          <ImageReveal
            src={edaImages.flightVolumeMap}
            alt="Map showing flight volume distribution across US airports"
            caption="Flight volume by airport location"
          />
        </div>
      </div>

      {/* Sub-section 3: Correlation story */}
      <div class="discovery-item animate-fade-up">
        <div class="discovery-content">
          <h3 class="headline-subsection text-white mb-3">
            The Correlation Story
          </h3>
          <p class="body-default text-slate-300 mb-4">
            Feature correlation analysis reveals which variables have the strongest
            relationships with delays. Previous flight delays show the highest
            correlation—a delayed inbound flight means a delayed outbound.
          </p>
          <div class="insight-callout">
            <span class="insight-icon">🔗</span>
            <span class="insight-text">
              Aircraft utilization patterns create delay chains. The same plane
              serves multiple flights per day.
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="discovery-visual">
          <ImageReveal
            src={edaImages.correlation}
            alt="Correlation heatmap showing relationships between flight delay features"
            caption="Feature correlation matrix for delay prediction"
          />
        </div>
      </div>

      {/* Sub-section 4: Previous flight effect */}
      <div class="discovery-item reverse animate-fade-up">
        <div class="discovery-content">
          <h3 class="headline-subsection text-white mb-3">
            The Previous Flight Effect
          </h3>
          <p class="body-default text-slate-300 mb-4">
            The strongest predictor of delay is whether the previous flight on the
            same aircraft was delayed. This single feature captures operational
            dependencies that weather data alone cannot explain.
          </p>
          <div class="insight-callout accent">
            <span class="insight-icon">🎯</span>
            <span class="insight-text">
              <strong>DEP_DEL15_PREV</strong> becomes our most important feature,
              achieving 17%+ of total feature importance.
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="discovery-visual">
          <ImageReveal
            src={edaImages.delayPrevFlight}
            alt="Analysis showing correlation between previous flight delay and current flight delay"
            caption="Impact of previous flight delay status"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Transition to next section */}
    <div class="section-transition animate-fade-up">
      <p class="body-large text-slate-400 text-center">
        Armed with these insights, we designed a prediction pipeline.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Container>
</Section>

<style>
  .discovery-grid {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4rem;
  }

  .discovery-item {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .discovery-item {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.2fr;
      gap: 3rem;
    }

    .discovery-item.reverse {
      grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr;
    }

    .discovery-item.reverse .discovery-content {
      order: 2;
    }

    .discovery-item.reverse .discovery-visual {
      order: 1;
    }
  }

  .discovery-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .discovery-visual {
    width: 100%;
  }

  .insight-callout {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    background: rgba(79, 195, 247, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid rgba(79, 195, 247, 0.15);
    margin-top: auto;
  }

  .insight-callout.accent {
    background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.05);
    border-color: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.2);
  }

  .insight-icon {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .insight-text {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-slate-300);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .section-transition {
    margin-top: 4rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
  }
</style>
